# Keep documentation and source diffable as text; guard against binary-flagged
# markdown (a past NUL-byte corruption made EDIT_LOG.md read as binary — DATA-02).
*.md text
*.ts text
*.tsx text
*.css text
*.json text

# Force LF regardless of local core.autocrlf: this file is read via Vite's
# `?raw` loader (src/branding/organization.ts) and its literal bytes —
# including line endings — are embedded verbatim into generated report HTML.
# Without a pinned eol, a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true silently bakes
# CRLF into that embedded SVG, which then mismatches any golden snapshot test
# run against a Linux (LF) checkout, e.g. CI (2026-07-29 edit log).
*.svg text eol=lf
